A12. execute_schedule_dispatch shift_candidate_alpha ?vehicle dispatch_slot_alpha (needs dispatch_allocated, candidate_vehicle_linked, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked, not dispatched)

Now after dispatch, vehicle becomes available again, dispatch_slot becomes available.

Now we need to ensure we have the vehicle available for each step. We'll need to allocate vehicle for each candidate before attach_task_profile etc. We can reuse same vehicle across candidates if we release after dispatch? There is no release vehicle action; vehicle becomes available only after dispatch. So we cannot allocate vehicle to a new candidate until we dispatch the previous one that used that vehicle. So we need to sequence: allocate vehicle to a candidate, prepare it, then dispatch it (which releases vehicle). Then we can allocate vehicle to next candidate.

