Shift_candidate_beta: need operator linked for goal; we can keep it linked until end (no need to release). So we will assign operator to shift_candidate_beta last and keep it.

Thus we need to allocate operator multiple times: assign, use, release, assign again, etc.

Now skill certificate: need to assign to shift_candidate_beta only (goal). So we assign skill_certificate_alpha to shift_candidate_beta and keep it linked.

Now compliance certificate: we need to assign to shift_candidate_alpha for verification, then verify, then finalize, then release to make it available again. So we will assign, verify, finalize, release.

